-- INDEPENDENT TESTS for the Legislation Act 2019 (NZ) encoding.
-- Every expected value below was first decided from the text of the Act and written in ANSWERS.md (not kept in this folder) BEFORE any .l4 file was opened.
-- Scenario numbers (S#) refer to ANSWERS.md. Seat questions are numbered ST#.
-- A failing assertion was a finding. Where triage afterwards changed an expected value, the `-- RECONCILED` comment above the assertion quotes the original and gives the reason; none is deleted.
-- The encoding's convention for "not covered" is NOTHING (MAYBE) or the constructor `The Act is silent`; for a case outside a section's own grant, duty or permission it answers JUST FALSE (fork F11, assumed, not ruled).

§ `Helpers (test-only; not law)`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
ymd y m d MEANS Date d m y

GIVEN w IS A DATE
      g IS A DATE
      e IS A DATE
      a IS A DATE
      s IS A DATE
      m IS A DATE
      l IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `Named day`
calOf w g e a s m l MEANS LIST
    `Named day` `Waitangi Day` w,
    `Named day` `Good Friday` g,
    `Named day` `Easter Monday` e,
    `Named day` `Anzac Day` a,
    `Named day` `the Sovereign's birthday` s,
    `Named day` `Matariki Observance Day` m,
    `Named day` `Labour Day` l

-- A year's calendar in which every named day falls on a weekday in 2020 (Waitangi 6 Feb Thu, Good Friday 10 Apr Fri, Easter Monday 13 Apr Mon, Anzac 24 Apr Fri, Sovereign's birthday 1 Jun Mon, Matariki 10 Jul Fri, Labour 26 Oct Mon).
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `Named day`
std y MEANS calOf (ymd y 2 6) (ymd y 4 10) (ymd y 4 13) (ymd y 4 24) (ymd y 6 1) (ymd y 7 10) (ymd y 10 26)

GIVEN x IS A `What the Act says of a word`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is silent` x MEANS x EQUALS `The Act is silent`

