-- S44 repeal includes expiry
#ASSERT `counts as repeal under section 13` `expiry` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- S44b repeal includes any other lapsing or ceasing of effect
#ASSERT `counts as repeal under section 13` `another lapsing or ceasing of effect` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- S45 revocation
#ASSERT `counts as repeal under section 13` `revocation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- S46 replacement
#ASSERT `counts as repeal under section 13` `replacement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- S47 an amendment, as such, is not a repeal under s 13 (my reading: "includes" is not "means", but an amendment is not named)
-- RECONCILED S47: reviewer wrote `#ASSERT `counts as repeal under section 13` `something else` EQUALS JUST FALSE`; triaged against the text: genuine fork (the test author's own verdict was fork, leaning to its own scenario being wrong): s 13 says repeal 'includes' expiry, revocation and replacement, and an 'includes' list excludes nothing, so an amendment as such is neither in nor out; the encoding answers NOTHING
#ASSERT `counts as repeal under section 13` `something else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- S48 person includes a corporation sole
#ASSERT `counts as a person under section 13` `a corporation sole` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- S49 a body corporate
#ASSERT `counts as a person under section 13` `a body corporate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- S50 an unincorporated body
#ASSERT `counts as a person under section 13` `an unincorporated body` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- S51 an ordinary individual is a person ("includes" is not exhaustive)
-- RECONCILED S51: reviewer wrote `#ASSERT `counts as a person under section 13` `a natural person` EQUALS JUST TRUE`; triaged against the text: genuine fork (the test author's verdict): s 13 says person 'includes' a corporation sole, a body corporate and an unincorporated body; the list is silent on an individual, ordinary meaning says yes, and the encoding has no ordinary-meaning layer, so it answers NOTHING
#ASSERT `counts as a person under section 13` `a natural person` EQUALS NOTHING
-- S52 New Zealand: the islands and territories within the Realm
#ASSERT `is within New Zealand as a territorial description` `another island or territory within the Realm of New Zealand`
#ASSERT `is within New Zealand as a territorial description` `the island commonly known as the North Island`
#ASSERT `is within New Zealand as a territorial description` `an island adjacent to the South Island`
-- S53-S56 the four exclusions, one by one
#ASSERT NOT `is within New Zealand as a territorial description` `the self-governing State of the Cook Islands`
#ASSERT NOT `is within New Zealand as a territorial description` `the self-governing State of Niue`
#ASSERT NOT `is within New Zealand as a territorial description` Tokelau
#ASSERT NOT `is within New Zealand as a territorial description` `the Ross Dependency`
-- S56b a place outside the Realm
#ASSERT NOT `is within New Zealand as a territorial description` `a place outside the Realm of New Zealand`
-- S57 territorial limits: the outer limits of the territorial sea
#ASSERT `the territorial limits of New Zealand are` EQUALS "the outer limits of the territorial sea of New Zealand"
-- S58 North Island includes adjacent islands
#ASSERT `which island the place is, under the Act's definitions` `an island adjacent to the North Island` EQUALS `North Island`
#ASSERT `which island the place is, under the Act's definitions` `the island commonly known as the North Island` EQUALS `North Island`
-- S59 South Island includes adjacent islands
#ASSERT `which island the place is, under the Act's definitions` `an island adjacent to the South Island` EQUALS `South Island`
#ASSERT `which island the place is, under the Act's definitions` `the island commonly known as the South Island` EQUALS `South Island`
-- S59b another island of the Realm is neither
#ASSERT `which island the place is, under the Act's definitions` `another island or territory within the Realm of New Zealand` EQUALS `Neither island`
